{
  "//": [
    "Composite indexes for every query this system runs.",
    "",
    "Scope is COLLECTION with a collectionGroup name, which covers the same",
    "collection under every trust and program — you never add indexes when a",
    "new trust or program is created.",
    "",
    "If a query is ever added without its index, Firestore fails with an error",
    "containing a one-click console link. Add the index HERE too, or the next",
    "deploy silently removes it.",
    "",
    "The fieldOverrides at the bottom are a real cost saving, not tidiness —",
    "see the note there.",
    "",
    "Do NOT list `__name__` in a field list. Firestore appends it to every",
    "composite index automatically, so an entry that spells it out is the SAME",
    "index as one that does not — and deploying both fails with",
    "HTTP 409 'index already exists'."
  ],
  "indexes": [
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "programId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "registrationNumber",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "programId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "status",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "registrationNumber",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "programId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "status",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "joinDateMs",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "programId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "joinDateMs",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "programId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "agentId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "dueAmount",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "programId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "agentId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "dueCount",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "registrationNumber",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": [
        "Receipt register — all receipts, newest first.",
        "",
        "The register also orders by `__name__` as a tie-break, because a bulk",
        "deposit writes forty receipts carrying the same `paidAtMs` and a cursor",
        "made of the timestamp alone would skip the other thirty-nine. Firestore",
        "appends `__name__` to every composite index automatically, so it is",
        "deliberately NOT listed here — spelling it out is the same index and",
        "the deploy fails with 409."
      ],
      "collectionGroup": "payments",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "paidAtMs",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "One member's receipts (the ledger drawer).",
      "collectionGroup": "payments",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "memberId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "paidAtMs",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "What one agent collected.",
      "collectionGroup": "payments",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "collectedByAgentId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "paidAtMs",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": [
        "revertClosing — who actually paid for closing #seq.",
        "This one index is why a revert touches a few hundred payers instead of",
        "deleting millions of rows the way the old system did."
      ],
      "collectionGroup": "payments",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "seqs",
          "arrayConfig": "CONTAINS"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "status",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "An agent's commission entries, newest first.",
      "collectionGroup": "commission_entries",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "agentId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "earnedAtMs",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "commission_entries",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "agentId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "status",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "earnedAtMs",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "commission_payouts",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "agentId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "paidAtMs",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "Agents list — active only, by name.",
      "collectionGroup": "agents",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "active",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "displayName",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "agents",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "displayName",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "Duplicate-phone check when adding an agent.",
      "collectionGroup": "agents",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "phone",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "programId",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "delete_flag",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "searchKeywords",
          "arrayConfig": "CONTAINS"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "fieldOverrides": [
    {
      "//": [
        "THIS IS A REAL COST SAVING, NOT HOUSEKEEPING.",
        "",
        "Firestore indexes every element of an array field separately. A member",
        "who has paid 300 closings out of order carries 300 entries in",
        "`paidSeqs` — so one write to that member would write 300 index entries",
        "as well, and index storage grows with it.",
        "",
        "We never query by paidSeqs; it is read as part of the member document",
        "and computed over in memory. So indexing it is pure waste, and turning",
        "it off makes every payment cheaper.",
        "",
        "Same for exemptSeqs, and for the display-only detail arrays."
      ],
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "fieldPath": "paidSeqs",
      "indexes": []
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "fieldPath": "exemptSeqs",
      "indexes": []
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "fieldPath": "extraDetails",
      "indexes": []
    },
    {
      "//": [
        "`items` holds the full receipt lines with names and amounts — never",
        "queried. `seqs` IS queried (array-contains, for revert), so it keeps",
        "its index; that is exactly why the two are separate fields."
      ],
      "collectionGroup": "payments",
      "fieldPath": "items",
      "indexes": []
    },
    {
      "//": "The shared index documents: one big array each, read whole, never queried.",
      "collectionGroup": "indexes",
      "fieldPath": "items",
      "indexes": []
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "programs",
      "fieldPath": "ageGroups",
      "indexes": []
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "programs",
      "fieldPath": "locationGroups",
      "indexes": []
    }
  ]
}
